  "id": "ex-05-adjektivdeklination-b1",
  "intro": "Standalone drill set, not tied to any lesson. Builds on the A2 set with what's left: the Nullartikel / \"starke\" declension — no article at all (frischer Fisch, kaltes Wasser), where the adjective carries the FULL der-word ending, including a Plural -e that is easy to confuse with the -en you learned after der/ein (gute Kinder, not guten Kinder — Nullartikel plural is the one place -e, not -en, shows up); the Genitiv adjective ending (-en almost everywhere, -er only in feminin/Plural); and multiple adjectives in a row, which all take the SAME ending. Blocks: A Basistraining → B Vertiefung → C Sprachbausteine → D Wiederholung. Answers in solutions.md.\n",
  "lesson": "EX/05-adjektivdeklination-b1",
  "level": "B1",
  "summary": null,
  "title": "Adjektivendungen ohne Artikel, im Genitiv & mehrere Adjektive — B1",
  "topic": "Adjektivdeklination (schwach, gemischt, stark)"
}
